;(По прибытии на место)
:'''Lingsha:''' All these years, and the view at the Alchemy Commission hasn't changed a bit.
:'''Lingsha:''' The tides come and go, but the ancient sea remains the same. For us Vidyadhara, there's nothing more nostalgic than our homeland.
:'''Dan Heng:''' ...You're a Luofu native, Miss Lingsha?
:'''Lingsha:''' Yes, I grew up here, listening to the sound of waves while researching prescriptions with my mentors and peers at the Alchemy Commission.
:'''Lingsha:''' It's kind of sad, isn't it? Everything changes but somehow remains familiar. Just like you, Dan Heng, I traveled far from home, and now I've returned. Seeing the familiar scenery brings back a hint of nostalgia.
:'''Yanqing:''' The view here would be even better without the Ambrosial Arbor.
:'''Lingsha:''' Oh, really? I think that towering tree looks pretty impressive.
:'''Yanqing:''' Even if it's impressive, it's a plaguemark. The Xianzhou have been fighting abominations for thousands of years, and now that the Ambrosial Arbor has been reborn, it's only natural for everyone to feel uneasy.
:'''Lingsha:''' Well, once a seed is planted, no matter how long it takes, it'll eventually sprout and bear fruit.
:'''Lingsha:''' In my humble opinion, the rebirth of the Ambrosial Arbor and the resurgence of the Disciples of Sanctus Medicus were inevitable. The seed was already planted when the ancestors of the Xianzhou sought immortality.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Why such a serious topic all of a sudden...?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} We can't just make wild speculations about these things, Miss Lingsha.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I thought we were here to have some tea, but where's the tea?
:'''Lingsha:''' My bad. Well, since you went through the entire Ambrosial Arbor Crisis firsthand, Dan Heng and Lieutenant Yanqing, I'd like to discuss something with you.
:{{tx}}
:{{tx}}
:'''Yunli:''' Why do I keep bumping into you? Are you stalking me or something?
:'''Yanqing:''' Of course not. Unlike you, Miss Yunli, I have important things to take care of. You, on the other hand, seem to have all the time in the world to wander around without returning my sword.
:'''Yunli:''' Grandpa used to say that a sword reflects its master. I talked to your sword, and it told me that you've been distracted. You hesitate when you should strike, and you struggle to stay calm when your sword is unsheathed...
:'''Yunli:''' Now that I see you again, I realize your sword was right. It wasn't me who took your sword. It was you who lost focus.
:'''Yanqing:''' Do you really expect me to believe that nonsense? I've been taking it easy on you because you're a guest from the Zhuming, but you're not taking the hint. Don't people from the Zhuming know you're supposed to return what you've borrowed?
:'''Yunli:''' Just look at this flying sword. Even if I give it back to you now, it'll just be taken away again in a few hours.
:'''Yunli:''' You know the Cloud Knight saying: "A Cloud Knight must never let slip their weapon," yes? Well, sure, I can give it back to you now, but on the battlefield, that's a whole different story. Poor flying sword.
:'''Yanqing:''' Fine, you don't have to give it back because I'll take it back myself!!
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Maybe I should call the general...
::'''(Trailblazer):''' But which general should I call?
::'''March 7th:''' Between these two, who do you think is tougher? Don't get me wrong, I'm just curious.
::Oh, to be young and at the whim of impulse.
::'''March 7th:''' Between these two, who do you think is tougher? Don't get me wrong, I'm just curious.
::'''Dan Heng:''' Get ready to separate them.
::So, is this the Wardance?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Oh, to be young and at the whim of impulse.
::'''March 7th:''' Between these two, who do you think is tougher? Don't get me wrong, I'm just curious.
::'''Dan Heng:''' Get ready to separate them.
::So, is this the Wardance?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} So, is this the Wardance?
:'''March 7th:''' Between these two, who do you think is tougher, Dan Heng? Don't get me wrong, I'm just curious.
:'''Dan Heng:''' Get ready to separate them.
:'''Lingsha:''' It is my first day at the Alchemy Commission &mdash; a brawl is definitely not how I imagined celebrating it.
:'''Yunli:''' Well, since you don't approve, I won't draw my sword here.
:'''Lingsha:''' I didn't mean it that way. Since you've already drawn your swords, you'd be disappointed if you didn't get to test one another, right?
:'''Lingsha:''' I've received reports that the delves near the Alchemy Commission are still infested with abominations. Seems like my predecessors left quite a mess. So, if you two want to determine who's better, why not focus on them instead of each other?
:'''Yunli:''' Clearing out some abominations? Meh, sounds boring.
:'''Yanqing:''' It's the Cloud Knights' duty to eliminate those abominations. You don't have to ask me twice, Miss Lingsha. I'll help you get rid of them.
:'''Yunli:''' Oh, you think you're the only one who knows how to behave? If Lingsha needs anything, I'll gladly draw my sword and help her out.
:'''Lingsha:''' It's so heartwarming to see both of you being so sweet and caring. So then, shall we get going?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Let's go!
